Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:03:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] :white_check_mark: Windows platform smoke check on the
 host GPU

os::gpu_import_smoke (doc-hidden): guest pages from allocate_aliasable viewed backwards through remap_runs_shared_overwrite, imported by import_view and host_memory into a no-copy buffer, filled by a blit, checked in the guest's own pages. A program runs it (the crate's tests need core's testkit, which is Unix's); os/windows/tests.rs holds the Windows test helpers and the Mach-rules test for when the testkit builds.

Verified: SMOKE OK on an RTX 5060, imported by pointer (no copy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
